#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
curant-cli — the local Curant client AND brain.

This is a deliberate architecture change from earlier versions: the
Curant server now knows almost nothing about any customer (just
license/billing — see server/app.py). Everything that makes a Curant
feel like *your* Curant — its persona, your standing instructions, the
people who matter to you, what it's learned about you over time, recent
conversation, and your own Anthropic API key — lives here, locally, on
your Mac. Claude is called directly from this machine; nothing about a
conversation is ever sent to Curant's own server.

What this script does:
  1. Activate a license key against the server (billing/entitlement only)
  2. Store your own Anthropic API key locally (never sent to the server)
  3. Relay incoming messages: build the system prompt from local
     persona/instructions/memories/important-people, call Claude directly,
     save the exchange locally, and extract any new long-term memories
  4. Decide whether a proactive check-in is warranted, using the same
     local context

NOTE ON WHAT'S "SAFE TO READ" HERE: earlier versions of this file were
intentionally inert — all product logic lived server-side, so there was
nothing sensitive to see by reading the client. That's no longer true.
Personas, the memory-extraction prompt, and the proactivity logic are
now all in this file. Treat this file itself as containing real product
IP — it should not be published as freely as the old "dumb client" was.
"""

